  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets during the week. 12 of the bouquets sold that week were sunflower bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To find the percentage of sales from sunflower bouquets:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Faraday owns a flower shop.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "That correction does not change the calculation. Faraday sold 50 bouquets, of which 12 were sunflower bouquets:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many sunflower bouquets did Faraday sell per day on average during that week? Additionally, Faraday's flower shop was open for 6 days during that week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday sold 12 sunflower bouquets over 6 days. The average per day was:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{6}=2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ sunflower bouquets per day}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $3 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Noted: individual sunflowers sell for **$3 each**. To calculate the revenue from individual sunflowers, we would also need to know how many individual sunflowers Faraday sold.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many sunflowers was Faraday able to sell after three days? And here are a few things you should know: Faraday sells bouquets of sunflowers for $8 each. Faraday earns $26 per day from individual sunflowers and $56 per day from bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Individual sunflowers generate:\n\n\\[\n\\$26 \\times 3=\\$78\n\\]\n\nAt \\(\\$3\\) per sunflower:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$78}{\\$3}=26\n\\]\n\nSo, Faraday sold:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{26\\text{ individual sunflowers}}\n\\]\n\nFor reference, the bouquet revenue corresponds to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$56}{\\$8}=7\\text{ bouquets per day}\n\\]\n\nor \\(21\\) bouquets after three days. The number of individual flowers in those bouquets cannot be determined without knowing how many sunflowers each bouquet contains.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over 3 days:\n\n- Individual sunflowers:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$26}{\\$3} \\times 3 = 26 \\text{ sunflowers}\n\\]\n\n- Bouquets sold:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$56}{\\$8} \\times 3 = 21 \\text{ bouquets}\n\\]\n\nEach bouquet has 12 sunflowers:\n\n\\[\n21 \\times 12 = 252 \\text{ sunflowers}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of sunflowers sold was:\n\n\\[\n26+252=\\boxed{278\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]\n\n",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $2 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Using the corrected price of **$2 per individual sunflower**:\n\n- Individual sunflowers sold in 3 days:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$26}{\\$2}\\times 3=13\\times 3=39\n\\]\n\n- Sunflower bouquets sold in 3 days:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$56}{\\$8}\\times 3=7\\times 3=21\n\\]\n\n- Sunflowers in those bouquets:\n\n\\[\n21\\times 12=252\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of sunflowers sold was:\n\n\\[\n39+252=\\boxed{291\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
